<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishme-Dagan I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishme-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagan">Dagan</a> I was the elder son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamshi-adad-i">Shamshi-Adad I</a>, the Amorite ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia">Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia</a>, in the 18th century BCE. His father installed him as king at Ekallatum on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasmah-addu">Yasmah-Addu</a> ruled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a>. After Shamshi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Adad</a>'s death the realm broke apart, and Ishme-Dagan held only Ekallatum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> competed for the region.</p></div>
